<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed clashes have erupted in the capital Yaounde, the port city Douala and the northern city Maroua, extending the Anglophone Crisis beyond the Northwest and Southwest regions. The fighting continues between Cameroonian security forces and Ambazonian separatists, the insurgency that began after the 2016‑17 protest suppression. These incidents show a geographic expansion from earlier reports that focused on isolated attacks within the Anglophone zones. The conflict’s intensity remains high, with 231 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;RNZ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;WDBJ7&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Euromaidan Press&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxOeWl5T19jdUplT1Vid0pVSWtDN2ZaWXlWSk9LWEFpQUc2ekVkNEdGV0NveUNpeWpfSFR2OUlYT0VHcHBWcmpTZWtZMW1OWnZET0J6QW9xQTJFV0JCTFJER01uMUl3cVNfdEdQRVM0SGVLOG1XYTU2VDdEMTExOG12MWRmWUJQRThVem5raFVSRWQ3LXZGajNTRHVnSlFBcXJJNUIxenJGaw?oc=5&quot;&gt;IOL&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Thought Catalog&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
